# Traefik safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized Traefik turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when the
turn never touches Traefik.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when Traefik is authorized:

- Listing routers, services, middlewares, entrypoints, IngressRoutes
- Reading CR YAML / file-provider snippets / Docker labels
- Explaining a rule match or middleware chain from evidence

Do **not** mutate unless the user gave an explicit verb **this turn** naming
the target object (router, service, middleware, IngressRoute, TLS option).

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn |
| --- | --- |
| Delete router / service / middleware / IngressRoute | **delete** + object name (+ namespace if CR) |
| Expose entrypoint or router without TLS | **expose** / **insecure** / **disable TLS** + named entrypoint or router |
| Drop TLS / clear cert secret or certresolver | **remove TLS** / **clear cert** + named router or IngressRoute |
| Remove auth / IP allowlist / forwardAuth middleware | **remove** / **drop** + middleware name + router |
| Point production host at new upstream | **point** / **retarget** / **change service** + host or router + new service |
| Broad catch-all rule (`HostRegexp` / Path `/`) on public entrypoint | **create** / **widen** + explicit acknowledgment of catch-all scope |

Ambiguous scope (e.g. "clean up old routers") → ask once for names; do not
mass-delete without listed targets.

## Prefer update-in-place

Prefer patching rule, service, middleware refs, or TLS block on the existing
object. Delete+recreate only when the user asked to replace or the provider
cannot update the field in place — state why in the receipt.

## Refuse

- Pasting Traefik dashboard credentials, basic-auth password hashes, ACME
  account private keys, or TLS private keys into chat
- Inventing router, middleware, IngressRoute, or entrypoint names
- Opening `web` (cleartext) as the only public entrypoint when the user did
  not ask to go insecure
- Absorbing another reverse-proxy product’s API/UI into this surface
- Inventing MCP tool names when no Traefik MCP is connected

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory: IngressRoute `app-web` ns `default`, match
`Host(\`app.example.com\`) && PathPrefix(\`/\`)`, entryPoints `websecure`,
service `app:80`, TLS secret name `app-tls` — no mutate.

Authorized retarget: stated host `app.example.com`; updated IngressRoute
`app-web` service → `app-v2:80`; middleware chain unchanged — no secrets.

